  "description": "Bean qou-oots. Derives what the depth-stratified binding functional Phi_k = SUM_{depth k} w_l log(|chi^l| d_q l) REQUIRES of its weight family, then prunes the four live candidates and re-runs the k=3 FR-pullback sweep under each. Three requirements, each with a Lean companion in QOU/BraidKnot/DepthStratifiedWeightRequirements.lean: R1 full support on the stratum (phi_eq_zero_of_weights_vanish) - excludes y_lambda, whose SU(2) row cap makes it EXACTLY zero on every stratum of depth >= 2, so Phi_3 is identically zero and the depth-3 chirality channel is vacuous; R2 n-independent total mass (crossRatio_smul) - excludes d_q^2/[n]_q!, whose mass drifts with n and so distorts every cross-nucleus comparison; R3 NO Markov requirement (phiDiff_eq_sum_log_ratio: the d_q inside the log cancels in the observable, so B is a weighted mean of log character-ratios and is not a trace) - which removes y_lambda's only claim to privilege here and makes the regular-trace z=0 exclusion of q_plancherel_vs_y_lambda_probe inapplicable, that exclusion being scoped to the linear trace evaluation z = tr(sigma_1). Two survive: d_q^2/D^2 (normalised BY CONSTRUCTION - no evidence, bean qou-sf1t) and the Molien family f^l q^{-kappa_l} d_q(l)/[n]_q! (normalised by THEOREM, molienSum_eq_qFactorial, sorry-free for all n and all q>1). New identification proved here exactly in Q(q): the Molien family IS the Feray-Meliot q-Plancherel measure of arxiv-1001.2180v2 under the corpus's own Q = q^2 bridge. The k=3 knot ranking is INVARIANT across all three families that can score it, so the choice does not move that conclusion - only its magnitudes.",
