    "verdict": "Two of four survive R1-R3: d_q^2/D^2 and the Molien family. The choice between them is NOT settled here. The evidential asymmetry is structural - d_q^2/D^2 is mass-one BY CONSTRUCTION (self-normalised, which bean qou-sf1t records as no evidence at all), whereas the Molien family's mass-one is a THEOREM whose normaliser [n]_q! was named independently, and which coincides exactly with the literature's q-Plancherel measure. That favours Molien and does not prove it. AND THE CHOICE IS EMPIRICALLY LOAD-BEARING: the k=3 knot ranking is NOT invariant - the three scoreable families name three DIFFERENT best knots (textbook 4_1 < 5_2 < 6_1; self-normalised 6_1 < 4_1 < 5_2; Molien 5_2 < 4_1 < 6_1), and under Molien the paper's named 6_1 is the WORST of the three and the only one failing to beat its own no-FR baseline. So the k=3 verdict is a statement about the weight family as much as about the knot, and no reading of it is safe until the family is derived."
